marches_dram_pages:
        It writes to the starting addresses of all pages and reads data from those addresses.
                                                                                                                            
marches_dram_full:
		It  writes every word in memory during the write phase, and then reads from those 
        words after the write phase completes.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

naive_marches:
        it performs a march test on the SRAM0 region from 0x40000000 to 0x4003FFFF.

marches_dram:
        it performs a March test on the SRAM region. During the write phase, it writes
        the address value to every 32-bit word in the SRAM, and during the read phase,
        it reads back every word and verifies it against the expected address value.



